Z||000000||MR2KLR||12-06-2001||07:39 PM||||<BR>My new (to me) 88 coupe dosen't have Power locks, Windows or Mirrors. However my 84 Parts car (SE) has it all does the harness have to be cut or can I unpulg it somewhere in the car? If I need to cut it I'd then need to splice all of the wires back togeter (  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> )<P>------------------<BR>  <BR>Black 88 Coupe: 120 MPH spedo, Aux. gauge pod, 195/55VR14 Potenza RE-71 tires, GT exhaust & ground F/X Soon to have 16" White Beretta GTZ W/ 215/45ZR16's<BR><A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOY/" TARGET=_blank>Tom's Page</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rodrv6||12-06-2001||08:18 PM||||The wire harness for the power stuff on the doors is seperate from the main harness in the car.  There is a plug for each door behind the carpet under the corners of the dash.  You can unplug the door harnesses there and remove the doors without cutting any wires.  The plugs may be a little hard to find as they may be tucked in to an access hole in the sheetmetal behind the carpet.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
